<title>USA: Pentair sees double-digit sales, net rises.</title>
<headline>Pentair sees double-digit sales, net rises.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PAUL, Minn. 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pentair Inc, a diversified manufacturer, said it expects to continue its record of double-digit percentage growth in sales and earnings.</p>
<p>Earlier, Pentair reported first quarter earnings of $0.48 a primary share, up from $0.40 a year ago. Sales were $411.1 million, up from $366.3 million.</p>
<p>&quot;Pentair's North American operations continue to perform very well, and with the slow but steady improvements expected in the European economic situation, we remain confident Pentair can continue its record of double digit sales and earnings increases,&quot; Winslow Buxton, chairman, said in a statement.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
